00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.050
SPEAKER: We've created a simple
Hello World app for Python

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.425
so you can quickly get a feel
for deploying an App Engine

00:00:09.425 --> 00:00:11.446
standard app to
Google Cloud platform.

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:13.820
Before I started, I made sure
to install the Google Cloud

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.620
SDK and the App Engine
Python components locally.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.090
In the Cloud console,
make a new GCP project

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.460
and create an App
Engine application.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.940
Choose the region closest to
you, in my case, US East 1.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.680
I'm going to do this
project in Python,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.470
and a standard App Engine
instance works great.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.950
First I locally clone the Hello
World Python app from GitHub.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.470
Everything you need is in a
Python doc sample directory,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.940
including this
minimal Python file

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.130
to handle the response
to the HTTP request.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.980
The simple YAML
file included starts

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.710
the app, which you can
view on local host.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.530
Start the app and then test
it by visiting localhost:8080

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.760
to see that it's working.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:50.420
Hooray!

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.511
You have Hello, World.

00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:53.510
Now you can leave the
development server running

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.640
and make changes that'll
be automatically detected.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.410
The server will
reload automatically

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.360
after I make any code changes.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.550
Let's change the text
in main.py and watch.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.420
Good morning.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.759
To deploy to App Engine,
run "gcloud app deploy."

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:11.550
It picks up the project
you created earlier

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.215
and will upload all the
relevant files to GCP.

00:01:14.215 --> 00:01:15.840
Once that's finished,
you can check out

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.881
the app in your browser
with "gcloud app browse."

00:01:20.232 --> 00:01:21.690
And now you're live
on appspot.com.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.800
Congratulations!

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.300
That's it.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.049
You've deployed your
first App Engine app.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:29.780
[MUSIC PLAYING]

